streamline provides the NVIDIA Streamline SDK (DLSS Super Resolution + Ray Reconstruction).

Spectrum consumes it via Sharpmake, not CMake, and does NOT link sl.interposer.lib:

    // headers: <streamline/sl.h>, <streamline/sl_dlss.h>, <streamline/sl_dlss_d.h>
    // runtime: LoadLibrary("Streamline/sl.interposer.dll") + GetProcAddress

Integration mode is MANUAL HOOKING - slInit() + slSetD3DDevice() after the
engine creates its own device. D3D12CreateDevice / CreateDXGIFactory2 / the
swapchain are deliberately NOT proxied by sl.interposer. That is sufficient for
DLSS-SR and DLSS-RR; DLSS Frame Generation would require the full interposer
and a proxied swapchain.

All plugin and NGX DLLs are deployed to a "Streamline" subdirectory next to the
executable, not beside it. Because Windows does not search subdirectories for
statically imported DLLs, the interposer is loaded explicitly at runtime and
that same directory is handed to sl::Preferences::pathsToPlugins so it can find
sl.common / sl.dlss / sl.dlss_d and the nvngx_* models.

sl.interposer.lib is still installed by this port, so switching to a linked
(or delay-loaded) integration later needs no port change.

Debug builds get Streamline's "development" DLL set (verbose logging + imgui
overlay); release builds get the signed production set.
